<body>
    <h1>Use Case 2.1.6.6: Admin Selects Campaign Audience for Creates Campa=
ign Setup (Step-6)</h1>
    <div class=3D"Section1">
        <p><strong>User Story</strong></p>
<p>As an Admin, I want to select the target audience for my phishing simula=
tion campaign by either choosing from predefined user groups or creating cu=
stom user groups, so that I can target specific employees or teams for the =
campaign.</p>
<p><strong>Description</strong></p>
<p>This use case describes how the Admin selects the audience for a phishin=
g simulation campaign in Step 6 of the campaign setup. The admin has the op=
tion to select from predefined user groups (such as Low Risk, Medium Risk, =
High Risk, Remote Workers) or to create custom user groups by selecting emp=
loyees from a list. If the Admin opts to create a custom user group, they w=
ill be able to specify a group name, search for employees, and add them to =
the new group. After making their selections, the Admin can proceed to the =
next step in the campaign creation process.</p>
<p><strong>Actors</strong></p>
<ul>
<li>
<p><strong>Admin</strong>: Selects predefined or custom user groups for the=
 campaign audience.</p></li>
<li>
<p><strong>System</strong>: Displays predefined groups, allows for custom g=
roup creation, and stores selected groups for targeting in the campaign.</p=
></li>
</ul>
<p><strong>Preconditions</strong></p>
<ol start=3D"1">
<li>
<p>The Admin is logged in and at the <strong>Audience</strong> step in the =
<strong>Create New Campaign</strong> wizard.</p></li>
<li>
<p>The system is operational and can display predefined user groups and sup=
port custom user group creation.</p></li>
</ol>
<p><strong>Postconditions</strong></p>
<ol start=3D"1">
<li>
<p>The target audience (predefined or custom groups) is saved and assigned =
to the campaign.</p></li>
<li>
<p>The Admin can continue to the next step in the campaign creation process=
.</p></li>
</ol>
<p>&nbsp;</p>
<p><strong>Main Flow (Normal Success Scenario)</strong></p>
<p><strong>Step 1: Select Predefined User Groups</strong></p>
<ol start=3D"1">
<li>
<p>The Aspire Admin is presented with the option to select predefined user =
groups such as:</p>
<ul>
<li>
<p><strong>Low Risk Employees</strong></p></li>
<li>
<p><strong>Medium Risk Employees</strong></p></li>
<li>
<p><strong>High Risk Employees</strong></p></li>
</ul></li>
<li>
<p>The Admin checks the checkbox next to the relevant predefined group(s).<=
/p></li>
<li>
<p>The system displays the number of users within each predefined group.</p=
></li>
</ol>
<p><strong>Step 2: Choose Custom User Groups</strong></p>
<ol start=3D"1">
<li>
<p>The Aspire Admin selects the <strong>Use Custom User Groups</strong> che=
ckbox.</p></li>
<li>
<p>The system displays the <strong>Select Existing Custom User Groups</stro=
ng> option.</p></li>
<li>
<p>The Admin can select from existing custom user groups (e.g., <strong>Sal=
es Group</strong>, <strong>IT Department</strong>, <strong>Marketing Team</=
strong>) by clicking the checkbox next to the group name.</p></li>
<li>
<p>The Admin can also search for specific users within the custom groups by=
 typing in the search field.</p></li>
</ol>
<p><strong>Step 3: Create New Custom User Group</strong></p>
<ol start=3D"1">
<li>
<p>The Admin clicks the <strong>Create New Custom User Group</strong> butto=
n.</p></li>
<li>
<p>The system displays an interface where the Admin can enter a <strong>Gro=
up Name</strong> for the new custom group.</p></li>
<li>
<p>The Employees list must display the following five attributes for each u=
ser:</p></li>
</ol>
<p><strong>Data Fields to Display.</strong></p>
<ul>
<li>
<p><strong>Full Name</strong></p></li>
<li>
<p><strong>Email Address</strong></p></li>
<li>
<p><strong>Department Name</strong></p></li>
<li>
<p><strong>Manager Name</strong></p></li>
<li>
<p><strong>Phone Number</strong></p></li>
</ul>
<h3 id=3D"UseCase2.1.6.6:AdminSelectsCampaignAudienceforCreatesCampaignSetu=
p(Step-6)-DefaultDisplayLimit">Default Display Limit</h3>
<p>By default, the list should display <strong>20 users</strong> per page.<=
/p>
<h3 id=3D"UseCase2.1.6.6:AdminSelectsCampaignAudienceforCreatesCampaignSetu=
p(Step-6)-OptiontoChangeDisplayLimit">Option to Change Display Limit</h3>
<p>A control (e.g., a dropdown menu or selector) must be provided to allow =
the user to change the number of users displayed on the page. The available=
 options are:</p>
<ul>
<li>
<p><strong>20</strong> users per page</p></li>
<li>
<p><strong>40</strong> users per page</p></li>
<li>
<p><strong>60</strong> users per page</p></li>
<li>
<p><strong>80</strong> users per page</p></li>
<li>
<p><strong>100</strong> users per page</p></li>
</ul>
<h3 id=3D"UseCase2.1.6.6:AdminSelectsCampaignAudienceforCreatesCampaignSetu=
p(Step-6)-PaginationImplementation">Pagination Implementation</h3>
<p>The application needs to implement <strong>server-side pagination</stron=
g> to manage large datasets efficiently.</p>
<ul>
<li>
<p><strong>Core Logic:</strong> The pagination mechanism should load the <s=
trong>next set of 20 users</strong> when triggered (e.g., by clicking a "Ne=
xt" button).</p></li>
<li>
<p><strong>Data Consistency:</strong> This step-by-step loading ensures tha=
t the initial request is fast and subsequent data is loaded only when neces=
sary. The <em>actual number of users loaded</em> (20, 40, 60, etc.) will be=
 determined by the limit selected in above Requirement.</p></li>
</ul>
<blockquote>
<p><strong>Example:</strong> If the user selects <strong>40</strong> users =
per page, the first page will show 40 users. When the user clicks "Next," t=
he application will load and display the next 40 users (users 41-80). Howev=
er, the <em>size of the data transfer</em> for each page load will correspo=
nd to the selected limit. If the current limit is 40, the next <em>page</em=
> will fetch 40. The mention of "next set of 20 users each time" suggests a=
 <strong>fixed step size</strong> for scrolling/loading, which might contra=
dict the dynamic limit options. Assuming the <strong>page size</strong> is =
the primary control, the system should load the selected limit (20, 40, 60,=
 etc.) on each page request.</p>
</blockquote>
<ol start=3D"4">
<li>
<p>The Admin can <strong>search </strong>for employees by name or departmen=
t or email address and add them to the new custom group.</p></li>
<li>
<p>The Admin can <strong>filter </strong>for employees by department or man=
ager name and add them to the new custom group.</p></li>
<li>
<p>The Admin clicks <strong>Save</strong> to create the custom group.</p></=
li>
<li>
<p>The newly created custom user group is now available for selection in th=
e audience list.</p></li>
</ol>
<p><strong>Step 4: Finalize Audience Selection</strong></p>
<ol start=3D"1">
<li>
<p>The Admin can review the selected user groups (predefined or custom).</p=
></li>
<li>
<p>The Admin clicks <strong>Save &amp; Continue</strong> to save the select=
ed audience and proceed to the next step in the campaign setup process.</p>=
</li>
</ol>
<p>&nbsp;</p>
<p><strong>Frontend Form Validation</strong></p>
<p><strong>Field Validation Rules</strong></p>
<ol start=3D"1">
<li>
<p><strong>Group Name Field (for Custom User Groups)</strong>:</p>
<ul>
<li>
<p><strong>Required</strong>: This field is mandatory when creating a custo=
m group.</p></li>
<li>
<p><strong>Validation</strong>:</p>
<ul>
<li>
<p>Must be at least 3 characters long.</p></li>
</ul></li>
<li>
<p><strong>Error Message</strong>: "Group name is required and must be at l=
east 3 characters."</p></li>
</ul></li>
<li>
<p><strong>Employee Selection</strong>:</p>
<ul>
<li>
<p><strong>Required</strong>: At least five employees must be added to a cu=
stom user group.</p></li>
<li>
<p><strong>Validation</strong>:</p>
<ul>
<li>
<p>The Admin must select employees from the search results.</p></li>
</ul></li>
<li>
<p><strong>Error Message</strong>: "Please select at least five employees f=
or the group."</p></li>
</ul></li>
<li>
<p><strong>User Group Selection</strong>:</p>
<ul>
<li>
<p><strong>Required</strong>: The Admin must select at least one predefined=
 or custom user group.</p></li>
<li>
<p><strong>Validation</strong>:</p>
<ul>
<li>
<p>Must not be empty.</p></li>
</ul></li>
<li>
<p><strong>Error Message</strong>: "Please select a user group."</p></li>
</ul></li>
</ol>
<p>&nbsp;</p>
<p><strong>Business Rules</strong></p>
<div class=3D"table-wrap">
<table data-table-width=3D"760" data-layout=3D"default" data-local-id=3D"87=
cba15f-448e-4e01-863b-0d62b8689ba7" class=3D"confluenceTable">
<tbody>
<tr>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p><strong>ID</strong></p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p><strong>Rule</strong></p></td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>BR-1</p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>Admin must select at least one predefined or custom user group.</p></td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>BR-2</p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>Admin can create custom user groups by adding employees manually or sele=
cting from existing groups.</p></td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>BR-3</p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>Tags and groups can be filtered and customized by departments, teams, or=
 risk levels.</p></td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>BR-4</p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>Custom user groups must have a name and contain at least one employee.</=
p></td>
</tr>
</tbody>
</table>
</div>
<p>&nbsp;</p>
<p><strong>Acceptance Criteria</strong></p>
<div class=3D"table-wrap">
<table data-table-width=3D"760" data-layout=3D"default" data-local-id=3D"67=
8c6ac7-906d-491c-942f-f709bb92903e" class=3D"confluenceTable">
<tbody>
<tr>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p><strong>ID</strong></p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p><strong>Acceptance Criteria</strong></p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p><strong>Pass/Fail Condition</strong></p></td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>AC-01</p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>Admin can select predefined user groups (e.g., Low Risk, High Risk).</p>=
</td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>Predefined groups are selectable and can be checked.</p></td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>AC-02</p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>Admin can select custom user groups from existing groups.</p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>Custom groups are displayed and selectable.</p></td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>AC-03</p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>Admin can search for employees within custom groups.</p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>Employee search functionality works correctly.</p></td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>AC-04</p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>Admin can create a new custom user group by entering a group name and se=
lecting employees.</p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>New group is created and saved successfully.</p></td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>AC-05</p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>Admin must assign at least one group (either predefined or custom) befor=
e proceeding.</p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>The <strong>Save &amp; Continue</strong> button is enabled only after se=
lection.</p></td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>AC-06</p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>Admin can remove any custom user group by clicking the <strong>Delete</s=
trong> icon next to the group.</p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>Custom groups can be removed from the list.</p></td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>AC-07</p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>Admin can filter custom user groups by category (e.g., department, team)=
.</p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>Filtering by category works correctly.</p></td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>AC-08</p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>Admin can create and assign multiple custom user groups in a single camp=
aign.</p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>Multiple groups can be selected and assigned at once.</p></td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>AC-09</p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>Admin can see the number of users within each predefined group.</p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>Number of users is displayed for each predefined group.</p></td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>AC-10</p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>Admin can click <strong>Create New Custom User Group</strong> and it pro=
mpts the Admin to enter a group name.</p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p><strong>Create New Custom User Group</strong> button works and prompts c=
orrectly.</p></td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>AC-11</p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>Admin can select employees from a list when creating a custom user group=
.</p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>Employees can be selected from a searchable list.</p></td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>AC-12</p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>Admin can proceed to the next step once at least one group is selected.<=
/p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p><strong>Save &amp; Continue</strong> button is only enabled after select=
ing a group.</p></td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>AC-13</p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>Admin can view the custom group details, such as group name and the numb=
er of users within the group.</p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>Custom group details are displayed correctly.</p></td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>AC-14</p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>Admin can search for groups by name or tag.</p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>Groups can be searched and filtered effectively.</p></td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>AC-15</p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>Admin can select more than one predefined or custom group to assign to t=
he campaign.</p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>Multiple groups can be selected simultaneously.</p></td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>AC-16</p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>The <strong>Create New Custom User Group</strong> button allows the Admi=
n to define the group name and select users.</p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p><strong>Create New Custom User Group</strong> button works properly.</p>=
</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>AC-17</p></td>
